WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.635
In 1919, the Paris Peace Conference made its decision.

00:00:03.635 --> 00:00:07.366
The arrangement on the Shandong issue deeply disappointed the Chinese people.

00:00:07.366 --> 00:00:12.389
The diplomats argued their case at the conference but failed.

00:00:12.389 --> 00:00:15.483
On May 4, students in Beijing took to the streets.

00:00:15.483 --> 00:00:18.387
They protested the Paris Peace Conference's arrangement for Shandong.

00:00:18.387 --> 00:00:22.000
More than 3,000 students gathered in front of the square.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.180
The march passed along long streets, and citizens rallied in support.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:30.076
Merchants also closed their shops to support the students' action.

00:00:30.076 --> 00:00:33.315
The movement also promoted the spread of vernacular Chinese.

00:00:33.315 --> 00:00:37.037
New newspapers and books were read by more and more people.

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:40.555
Writers wrote new works in vernacular Chinese.

00:00:40.555 --> 00:00:43.706
New ideas spread among young people.

00:00:43.706 --> 00:00:46.974
Everyone began to think about the future of the nation and its culture.

00:00:46.974 --> 00:00:50.552
Female students also came out to take part in public affairs.

00:00:50.552 --> 00:00:53.163
The May Fourth Movement influenced the entire era.

00:00:53.497 --> 00:00:56.428
It became an important page in modern Chinese history.
